additional-resources-in-this-postFull Dining Room Tour & Resources available HERE\n\n#### Full Living Room Tour & Resources available HERE\n\n#### Full Kitchen Tour & Resources available HERE--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClassic style family kitchen | British Institute of Interior Design (https://biid.org.uk/classic-style-family-kitchen)\nciteturn2search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; A neutral colour palette was softened by the warmer tones of polished nickel fittings and oak interiors in the cabinetry and we designed a bespoke breakfast cupboard for the family with a quartz countertop, concertina doors, and interior electrical sockets and lighting.\n\nJohn Lewis of Hungerford plc project\n\n# Classic style family kitchen\n\nSee John Lewis of Hungerford plc profile\n\nA substantial extension at the rear of our clients’ property allowed us to create a stunning family space that would play with scale and symmetry and meet their brief for a timeless farmhouse kitchen. We started with the clients’ wish list of appliances and storage choices and designed the kitchen around those elements using our Shaker design. To accentuate the sense of space, we created extrawide drawers and cabinets, left space at the end of each cabinet run instead of taking them right up to each wall and kept the wall cabinets free of any adjoining full height cabinets.\nA neutral colour palette was softened by the warmer tones of polished nickel fittings and oak interiors in the cabinetry and we designed a bespoke breakfast cupboard for the family with a quartz countertop, concertina doors, and interior electrical sockets and lighting.\n\n### Gallery\n\n  * Image\n\n>   * Image\n\n>   * Image\n\n>   * Image\n\n>   * Image\n\n>   * Image\n\n> [Input] [Input]--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBreakfast Pantry: Smart Storage to Declutter Your Kitchen (https://www.harveyjones.com/blog/planning/breakfast-pantry-smart-storage-to-declutter-your-kitchen)\nciteturn2search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: last month; A breakfast pantry is one of the most quietly transformative additions to a bespoke kitchen – a dedicated space that tucks away everything you need to start the day, then closes neatly behind beautiful doors when you don’t. ... Image: Multipurpose pantry ideal as a breakfast cupboard with worktop space, appliances and door storage\n\n# Breakfast Pantry: Smart Storage to Declutter Your Kitchen\n\n5th May 2026\n\nImage: Breakfast dresser with bespoke wooden shelves and wooden worktop for storing appliances and preparation\n\nPicture Monday morning: coffee not yet made, cereal boxes crowding the counter, someone hunting for the toaster behind the stand mixer.\n\nA breakfast pantry is one of the most quietly transformative additions to a bespoke kitchen – a dedicated space that tucks away everything you need to start the day, then closes neatly behind beautiful doors when you don’t. Think of it as your morning routine, zoned.\n\nWhether you’re drawn to the elegance of a full-height breakfast pantry cupboard with pocket doors, or a built-in breakfast station integrated beneath your upper cabinetry, there’s a solution to suit every household.\n\nIn this guide, we’ll walk you through everything: what a bespoke breakfast pantry is, how to design one well, and the details that make the difference between functional and truly special.\n\nDiscover real, bespoke kitchen & home inspiration.\n\nREQUEST YOUR BROCHURE\n\n## What is a Breakfast Pantry?\n\nA breakfast pantry is a self-contained section of kitchen cabinetry – typically a full-height or half-height cupboard. It’s dedicated to storing and preparing everything the household needs for breakfast. Open the doors and you’ll find a concealed worktop, space for kitchen appliances such as a kettle, toaster or coffee machine, and shelving for cereals, jars, cups and daily essentials.\n\nUnlike a pantry larder, the breakfast pantry is designed specifically around your morning routine. It keeps the main kitchen worktops clear and creates a dedicated zone for the your family to use. When the doors are closed, it leaves your kitchen looking clean and calm.\n\nYou may also see it called a breakfast cupboard, a breakfast station, or a breakfast dresser. The principles are the same: a purposeful, beautiful space that earns its place every single day.\n\nImage: Multipurpose pantry ideal as a breakfast cupboard with worktop space, appliances and door storage\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKitchen Tour | Bespoke Interior Alchemy | Davonport (https://www.davonport.com/kitchen-tour-bespoke-interior-alchemy/)\nciteturn2search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.1 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; 5 | The breakfast cupboard ... Featuring a convenient granite shelf to help keep food cool, as well as a variety of internal cupboards, drawers and even vegetable crates, this bespoke breakfast pantry provides storage for everything from coffee cups to the toaster and even breakfast pastries.\nFor a home designed to welcome the grown up children and their own families, ample refrigeration space was a necessity. Two Sub-Zero fridges, plus a freezer and two freezer drawers perfectly fit the bill. All this is beautifully encased by a walnut frame featuring the hand carved ‘cold store’ detailing as a finishing touch.\n\n5 | The breakfast cupboard\n\nThis breakfast cupboard is exemplary of well-considered design. With the pocket doors closed, it appears as simply two tall cupboards. However, upon opening the doors the breakfast cupboard is revealed. Featuring a convenient granite shelf to help keep food cool, as well as a variety of internal cupboards, drawers and even vegetable crates, this bespoke breakfast pantry provides storage for everything from coffee cups to the toaster and even breakfast pastries. And of course, when not in use, the doors are simply closed to disguise the storage within.\n\nVisit our Belgravia style page to view other projects inspired by this design. Or if you would like to discuss your own project plans with us please get in touch.\n\n### Author\n\nRichard Davonport\n\nManaging Director, Richard, founded Davonport in 1993. With over thirty years of experience, he oversees the day-to-day running of the company and works closely with every department. His commitment ensures that Davonport consistently delivers not only the finest handcrafted kitchens but also exceptional service to every customer.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLuxury Kitchen Designers | Clive Christian Interiors (https://www.clivechristianfurniture.com/room/kitchens/)\nciteturn2search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Start mornings in style with a bespoke breakfast cupboard.\nCharge devices wirelessly or via USB while entertaining and cook in a clutter‑free luxury kitchen.\n\nImage: Fine artisan kitchen cabinetry showcasing expertly crafted hardwood furniture design\n\n### Safe Drawer\n\nProtect car keys, wallets and other valuables in a secure safe drawer lined with anti‑cloning material and accessed via fingerprint sensor, an essential feature for a modern luxury kitchen.\n\nImage: Custom-built finely crafted kitchen cabinetry with classic timber finishes and integrated appliances\n\n### Bar Cabinet\n\nYour own luxury bar cabinet with fold‑away doors, bespoke shelving and integrated wine fridges. Elevate entertaining with a discreet bar cabinet within your bespoke kitchen.\n\nImage: Commissioned distinguished kitchen cabinetry with beautifully made dark wood doors and brass hardware detail\n\n### Breakfast Cupboard\n\nStart mornings in style with a bespoke breakfast cupboard. House your coffee machine, toaster and kettle behind elegant doors designed to harmonise with your luxury kitchen.\n\nImage: Exquisite artisan-made kitchen cabinetry display in showroom setting with made-to-order design\n\n### Knife Block Drawer\n\nSave counter space with a neatly designed knife block drawer, to store and protect your collection.\n\nImage: Handcrafted luxury kitchen cabinetry with bespoke wooden storage and elegant design details\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA classic in white: Family Kitchen by Martin Moore - The Kitchen Think (https://www.thekitchenthink.co.uk/a-classic-in-white-family-kitchen-by-martin-moore/)\nciteturn2search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; The bespoke breakfast cupboard is a total win according to the family!\nTo make better use of the space, we made several quite considerable changes. We reconfigured the layout and increased the height of the cupboards to improve the visual proportions. We also created a vertical pantry next to the Aga for maximum ease of use and practical storage. Any tricky nooks and crannies were all converted into useful storage.\n\nImage\n\nQ: What design elements do you think make the scheme so successful?\n\nI think the beauty of this kitchen ultimately lies in its simplicity – it isn’t overly fussy; however, the soft furnishings and the amazing Italian marble add just the right amount of interest and decorative flair. Soft furnishings are important, they add texture and softness to a scheme, and are useful acoustically, too.\n\nImage\n\nQ: Now the project is finished, what aspects are you and your clients most pleased with?\n\nThe bespoke breakfast cupboard is a total win according to the family! It’s positioned next to the island and designed to keep breakfast making facilities close at hand, so all that early morning activity is confined to just one area. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPREVIOUS PAGE: Framed Shaker cabinetry painted in Fossil (https://john-lewis.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/2022-kitchen-brochure.pdf)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.4 years ago; A neutral colour palette was softened by the warmer tones of polished nickel fittings and oak interiors in the cabinetry and we designed a bespoke breakfast cupboard for the family with a quartz countertop, concertina doors, and interior electrical sockets and lighting.\nPREVIOUS PAGE: Framed Shaker cabinetry painted in Fossil\n\nA substantial extension at the rear of our clients’ property allowed us to create a stunning family space that would play with scale and symmetry and meet their brief for a timeless farmhouse kitchen. We started with the clients’ wish list of appliances and storage choices and designed the kitchen around those elements using our Shaker design. To accentuate the sense of space, we created extra-wide drawers and cabinets, left space at the end of each cabinet run instead of taking them right up to each wall and kept the wall cabinets free of any adjoining full height cabinets.\n\nA neutral colour palette was softened by the warmer tones of polished nickel fittings and oak interiors in the cabinetry and we designed a bespoke breakfast cupboard for the family with a quartz countertop, concertina doors, and interior electrical sockets and lighting.\n\nThe purity of the design sits well within the space and provides an incredibly stylish and comfortable kitchen for the family to enjoy.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nLarge kitchen photograph showing pale Shaker-style cabinetry in a bright room with a tall cabinet run on the left, wall cabinets centered, a range cooker partly visible at right, a central island edge in the foreground, beige tiled floor, and a vase of flowers on the counter.\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e2\">\nSmall lower-left inset photo showing the cooking area: pale drawers and cabinets, a black-and-white range cooker with brass details, a shelf/hood above, and countertop styling with flowers and bottles.\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e3\">\nSmall lower-right inset photo showing the sink and window area: pale cabinetry, white sink and countertop, arched window, flowers on the counter, and a bright view outside.\n</visual_element>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPREVIOUS PAGE: Framed Shaker cabinetry painted in Fossil (https://www.john-lewis.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/New-2022-brochure.pdf)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.4 years ago; A neutral colour palette was softened by the warmer tones of polished nickel fittings and oak interiors in the cabinetry and we designed a bespoke breakfast cupboard for the family with a quartz countertop, concertina doors, and interior electrical sockets and lighting.\nPREVIOUS PAGE: Framed Shaker cabinetry painted in Fossil\n\nA substantial extension at the rear of our clients’ property allowed us to create a stunning family space that would play with scale and symmetry and meet their brief for a timeless farmhouse kitchen. We started with the clients’ wish list of appliances and storage choices and designed the kitchen around those elements using our Shaker design. To accentuate the sense of space, we created extra-wide drawers and cabinets, left space at the end of each cabinet run instead of taking them right up to each wall and kept the wall cabinets free of any adjoining full height cabinets.\n\nA neutral colour palette was softened by the warmer tones of polished nickel fittings and oak interiors in the cabinetry and we designed a bespoke breakfast cupboard for the family with a quartz countertop, concertina doors, and interior electrical sockets and lighting.\n\nThe purity of the design sits well within the space and provides an incredibly stylish and comfortable kitchen for the family to enjoy.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nLarge full-height photo of a bright farmhouse-style kitchen with pale Shaker cabinetry, tall pantry-style cupboards, a central wall cabinet, beige tiled floor, and a white island edge in the foreground; flowers, books, and a black range cooker are visible.\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e2\">\nSmall inset kitchen photo showing a pale countertop with a black range cooker, drawers with polished nickel handles, a vase of flowers, and a shelf/hood detail above.\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e3\">\nSmall inset kitchen photo showing pale cabinetry, a window, a sink in the foreground, flowers on the counter, and a bright dining/kitchen area with a dark-framed door or window at right.\n</visual_element>\n\nLATEST PROJECTS | 27--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHIGHFIELD FARM, SOUTH CLIFTON (https://media.rightmove.co.uk/16k/15670/155482769/15670_100005028555_DOC_00_0005.pdf)\nciteturn2search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; the home is the superb bespoke open plan breakfast kitchen, ... with bench seating and bespoke breakfast cupboard hosting\nlove getting out into the countryside, you will be able to enjoy walks along the banks of the river Trent. the road and within an approximate 2 minute drive/12 minute |  | \nlove getting out into the countryside, you will be able to enjoy walks along the banks of the river Trent. walk. For older children, Tuxford Academy (rated Good by Ofsted) |  | \nlove getting out into the countryside, you will be able to enjoy walks along the banks of the river Trent. is approximately 14 minutes away by car. |  | \nHighfield Farm nestles within generous grounds approximately \n0.35 acres in the heart of this highly desirable village.  The hub of \nthe home is the superb bespoke open plan breakfast kitchen, \nsuperbly appointed with bespoke units with wealth of features, \nquality appliance package, quartz worktops and substantial \ncoordinating central island.  Ample breakfasting area with fitted \nbench seating and breakfast cupboard. \nFAMILY/GARDEN ROOM 16’0” x 12’10” (4.87m x 3.92m) maximum \ndimensions, log burner, complemen